// Development ergonomics only. It lets the two modules be worked on together
// without a replace directive in either go.mod — which is what makes the nested
// module workable in practice (SERVER-DESIGN.md §9).
//
// It is committed on purpose. A replace directive would be committed too, but a
// replace directive ships to consumers; a workspace does not, because the go
// command ignores go.work in any module downloaded as a dependency.
//
// One consequence to know about: inside the workspace, imapserver builds
// against the root module's working tree, not against the version its go.mod
// requires. Verifying that the require line is honest therefore needs
// GOWORK=off. CI does exactly that; see .github/workflows/ci.yml.
go 1.24

use (
	.
	./imapserver
)
